  "description": "Open-loop EEG dataset of lower-limb kinesthetic motor imagery of ankle dorsiflexion and plantarflexion alternated with relaxation, recorded from six healthy participants. Each participant completed two sessions, one with a static and one with a motion lower-limb exoskeleton model. Data were recorded with 28 EEG channels plus EOG and auxiliary channels at 250 Hz and are provided in a BIDS-formatted derivative through MOABB.",
  "methods_description": "Participants performed cue-based (auditory) kinesthetic motor imagery of ankle dorsiflexion/plantarflexion alternating with rest, in trials of 4 s, over 11 runs per session in two sessions (static and motion exoskeleton). EEG was recorded at 250 Hz from 28 EEG channels with 4 EOG and 3 miscellaneous channels, using a standard_1005 montage.",
